From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:16:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm: carve the fallback vpl011 out of the extended regions

Companion to "vpl011: fall back to the guest layout when the Xen UART
region cannot be re-used".  That fallback places the emulated vpl011 at
GUEST_PL011_BASE for a direct-mapped domain, and for such a domain that
address by construction lies inside one of the holes
make_hypervisor_node() advertises as extended regions.

Linux's unpopulated-alloc claims section-sized (128MB) chunks of the
extended regions in the iomem resource tree.  The first chunk of the
region starting at 0x20000000 contains the vpl011 at 0x22000000, whose
resource the sbsa-uart driver has already claimed, so request_resource()
fails with EBUSY and privcmd foreign mappings fail:

    xen:xen_privcmd: alloc_empty_pages Could not alloc 10646 pfns rc:-16
    xc: panic: xg_dom_boot.c:156: xc_dom_boot_domU_map: failed to mmap
        domU pages 0x40000+0x2996 [mmap, errno=12]

i.e. the driver domain can build no guest at all.  Measured on the
Raspberry Pi 4 while creating DomA from DomD.

Carve a 2MB-aligned window around the vpl011 page out of the computed
extended regions before they are written to the guest DT.  2MB because
both edges of an extended region are kept 2MB aligned elsewhere in this
file.  Then drop the banks that became empty and re-sort the list:
arch_xen_unpopulated_init() (arch/arm/xen/enlighten.c) rejects the whole
list with -EINVAL as soon as it is not sorted and non-overlapping, and a
rejected list silently falls back to ballooning one page of driver-domain
RAM per foreign-mapped guest page, which on a 1-2GB DomD OOM-kills the
device model mid-boot.

On the board the window splits one region in the middle:

    (XEN) d1: carving vpl011 window 0x22000000->0x22200000 out of extended region 1
    (XEN) d1: extended region 1: 0x20000000->0x22000000
    (XEN) d1: extended region 2: 0x22200000->0x38000000

Changes from the version this was ported from: when the window covered
the head of a bank, the old code appended the remainder as a new tail
bank and then dropped "the duplicate" with nr_banks-- -- but when the
array was already full no tail had been appended, so it dropped an
unrelated bank instead and lost the remainder.  The remainder now stays
in the bank itself unless a tail was actually appended, and the tail is
copied from the whole bank (struct membank's type shares a union).
Covered by a host-side test of all eight cases (split, head, head with a
full array, tail, full cover, no overlap, split with a full array, no
vpl011); only the middle split is exercised on this board.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [only needed with 4.22-0011, which is itself
 Inappropriate]
---
 xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c | 105 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 105 insertions(+)

--- a/xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c
+++ b/xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c
@@ -1083,6 +1083,111 @@ int __init make_hypervisor_node(struct domain *d,
         if ( res )
             printk(XENLOG_WARNING "%pd: failed to allocate extended regions\n",
                    d);
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_SBSA_VUART_CONSOLE
+        /*
+         * When domain_vpl011_init() could not re-use the Xen console UART for
+         * a direct-mapped domain it places the emulated vpl011 at
+         * GUEST_PL011_BASE, which by construction lies inside one of the
+         * holes this function is about to advertise as extended regions.
+         * Linux's unpopulated-alloc then claims section-sized chunks of those
+         * regions in the iomem tree, collides with the already-claimed UART
+         * resource and fails with EBUSY, which surfaces as privcmd foreign
+         * mappings failing -- xl cannot build any guest from that domain.
+         * Measured on the Raspberry Pi 4 driver domain:
+         *     xen:xen_privcmd: alloc_empty_pages Could not alloc 10646 pfns rc:-16
+         * Carve a 2MB-aligned window around the vpl011 page out of the
+         * extended regions so the guest kernel never places scratch space on
+         * top of it. 2MB because both edges of an extended region are kept
+         * 2MB aligned elsewhere in this file.
+         */
+        if ( d->arch.vpl011.base_addr )
+        {
+            const uint64_t carve_s = d->arch.vpl011.base_addr & ~(MB(2) - 1);
+            const uint64_t carve_e = ROUNDUP(d->arch.vpl011.base_addr +
+                                             GUEST_PL011_SIZE, MB(2));
+            unsigned int j, nr = ext_regions->nr_banks;
+
+            for ( j = 0; j < nr; j++ )
+            {
+                struct membank *bank = &ext_regions->bank[j];
+                const uint64_t bank_e = bank->start + bank->size;
+                bool tail_added = false;
+
+                if ( carve_s >= bank_e || carve_e <= bank->start )
+                    continue;
+
+                printk("%pd: carving vpl011 window %#"PRIx64"->%#"PRIx64
+                       " out of extended region %u\n",
+                       d, carve_s, carve_e, j);
+
+                if ( carve_e < bank_e &&
+                     ext_regions->nr_banks < ext_regions->max_banks )
+                {
+                    struct membank *tail =
+                        &ext_regions->bank[ext_regions->nr_banks++];
+
+                    *tail = *bank;
+                    tail->start = carve_e;
+                    tail->size = bank_e - carve_e;
+                    tail_added = true;
+                }
+
+                if ( carve_s > bank->start )
+                    bank->size = carve_s - bank->start;
+                else if ( carve_e < bank_e && !tail_added )
+                {
+                    bank->start = carve_e;
+                    bank->size = bank_e - carve_e;
+                }
+                else
+                    /* Fully covered, or the tail bank now holds the rest. */
+                    bank->size = 0;
+            }
+
+            /*
+             * Linux requires the extended regions to be sorted by start
+             * address and non-overlapping: arch_xen_unpopulated_init() in
+             * arch/arm/xen/enlighten.c rejects the whole list with -EINVAL as
+             * soon as regs[i - 1].end + 1 > regs[i].start.  The split above
+             * appends the tail bank at the end of the array, which breaks that
+             * order.  A rejected list is not a soft failure: it makes
+             * xen_alloc_unpopulated_pages() fall back to the balloon, i.e. one
+             * page of driver-domain RAM per foreign-mapped guest page.  On the
+             * Raspberry Pi 4 (DomD has 1GB) that OOM-kills the device model
+             * mid-boot and the guest then hangs forever on an unanswered
+             * ioreq, with pause_flags=_VPF_blocked_in_xen.  Drop the empty
+             * banks and sort what is left.
+             */
+            for ( j = 0; j < ext_regions->nr_banks; )
+            {
+                if ( ext_regions->bank[j].size == 0 )
+                {
+                    unsigned int k;
+
+                    for ( k = j; k + 1 < ext_regions->nr_banks; k++ )
+                        ext_regions->bank[k] = ext_regions->bank[k + 1];
+                    ext_regions->nr_banks--;
+                }
+                else
+                    j++;
+            }
+
+            for ( j = 1; j < ext_regions->nr_banks; j++ )
+            {
+                const struct membank tmp = ext_regions->bank[j];
+                unsigned int k = j;
+
+                while ( k > 0 && ext_regions->bank[k - 1].start > tmp.start )
+                {
+                    ext_regions->bank[k] = ext_regions->bank[k - 1];
+                    k--;
+                }
+                ext_regions->bank[k] = tmp;
+            }
+        }
+#endif
+
         nr_ext_regions = ext_regions->nr_banks;
     }
 
